# Staff Scheduling page — `scheduling.html` (s3.1.34)

Resume: `@scheduling$` / `$schedule-for$`.

## Who it is for

A **satellite** for the owners of a work calendar: a DJ (their own bookings), a Club Admin / schedule manager (a club), or a promoter (a promoting company). Club Admins also have the Scheduling tab in `admin.html`; this page is the stand-alone version (DJs and promoters have no Club Admin). Master Admins may manage every owner — the server's `canManageOwner` (`functions/scheduling-functions.js`) already returns true for them. Workers confirm shifts under **My assignments** (worker notify links redirect to `patron-portal.html?tab=work-calendar`).

## Sign-in bug fixed in s3.1.34

`firebase-config.js` only sets `window.firebaseConfig`; it never calls `initializeApp`. `scheduling-portal.js` called `firebase.auth()` at load inside `try { } catch { return; }`, so with no app it **silently exited**: nothing bound, status stuck on "Restoring your FLOQR session…", badge on "checking…", Google button left visible. `FLOQRSessionShell.requireSignIn` also gave up after 4 s with no app. Role was never the cause.

Fix: page app runs `if (!firebase.apps.length) firebase.initializeApp(window.firebaseConfig)` before `firebase.auth()` (same as `services-app.js`, `pickup-app.js`), and shows a status on init failure. Every satellite page app must start Firebase itself.

Second bug: `data-floqr-auth-chrome` was on the Subscription card, so a signed-in user would lose the badge + Subscribe button (the shell hides auth chrome on sign-in). The chrome is now a separate row with a **Sign in** button → `popupBlocked` (iframe) / `redirectToLogin()` (general sign-in). No Google-only button.

## Schedule for picker

- Segmented radios `portalOwnerType`: `dj` (My DJ schedule) · `club` · `promoterCompany` — the only three `OWNER_TYPES` on the server.
- `<select id="portalOwnerId">` shows names; values keep the stored format: dj = uid (no input), club = `clubLocations` id, promoterCompany = `promoterCompany` text from the designation (server compares case-insensitively).
- Sources (`scheduling-owner-picker.js` mirrors `canManageOwner`): `users.clubAdminLocationIds`, active `clubAdminAssignments` (patronUid), `clubLocations` `adminUids` / `adminEmails`, `clubEmployeeDesignations` (workerUid) with Club Admin role or `manageSchedules`, not rejected. Companies: designation status active/approved/elected + promoter role.
- Master Admin (claim or verified listed email — UI hint only): every `clubLocations` doc (limit 1000) + distinct `promoterCompany` values, with a search box.
- `?owner=type:id` deep links still preselect; an id not in the lists stays selectable (club label fetched).
- Choosing an owner never writes. The old client write of `staffSchedulingPaid: 1` (demo) was removed; the server's entitlement resolver handles demo venues.

Help: `help-scheduling-schedule-for` on the **Schedule for** h2 (not the page h1), venueAdmin + serviceMember; in `functions/floqai-content-classes.json` (FloqAi shows it only after `getFloqAiAccess` is redeployed with that manifest). Test: `functions/scheduling-owner-picker.test.js`.

## Assign to picker (s3.1.35)

"Assignee uid / name" free text is gone. `<select id="portalAssignee">` lists people as **name · role** (search box above 8 rows, matches name/role/email, never uid). The option value is the uid, sent unchanged as `createScheduleShift.assigneeUid`; `assigneeName` comes from the picked row. Picking a person fills **Notify by email** / **Notify by SMS / WhatsApp** (editable). Pure helpers: `scheduling-assignee-picker.js` (`FLOQRScheduleAssignees`); test `functions/scheduling-assignee-picker.test.js`. `admin-scheduling.js` untouched (read for its roster query only).

| Owner | Roster (Firestore, rules-safe) | `getPeopleDirectory` |
|---|---|---|
| club | `clubEmployeeDesignations` where `clubLocationId == id` (club staff / Master Admin may read) | `mode: "club"`; non-Master keeps only affiliated rows (club mode adds a `phone` key only for people tied to the club) |
| promoterCompany | Master Admin: designations where `promoterCompany == id`. Others: designations at each club where they themselves promote for that company, filtered to the company (a direct company query is rejected by rules) | `mode: "services"` (+ `"public"` for Master Admin) |
| dj | — | `mode: "services"` (+ `"public"` for Master Admin) |

You are always listed first (`(you)`), then team, then everyone else. Rejected designations are skipped.

## Localization (s3.1.35)

Every label, placeholder and status on the page is a `sched.*` chrome key (11 packs), including `worker-confirm.js` (Select all / Approve selected / Decline selected) and `assignment-card.js` status labels (Draft / Pending / Confirmed / Unfilled) — both fall back to English when `FLOQRI18n` is not loaded (schedule-embed, Node tests). The subscription badge says **Paid this month / Not paid this month**; internal field names (`staffSchedulingPaid`) are never shown.

## Version links (s3.1.35)

The owner saw the old page at `scheduling.html?v=s3.1.26&from=floqai`: Pages served the new file for that URL; the browser showed its cached copy (Pages `max-age=600`) and the link came from a FloqAi tab opened before the s3.1.32 nav fix. Since s3.1.35 `floqai-help-repository.js` / `intent-search.js` read `FLOQRNav.appVersion` at call time with **no** fallback version (no nav → no `v`), pages load `floqr-nav.js` before them, and the bump script re-stamps static hub links. `functions/app-version-sync.test.js` fails on hardcoded `?v=` literals or version fallbacks in link builders, wrong script order, or stale hub links.

s3.1.36: a later screenshot showed `scheduling.html?&from=floqai` (empty `v`) on the s3.1.34 page. No builder in s3.1.34 or later can emit `?&` — all use `URLSearchParams` (worst case `v=&`) — so that address was the s3.1.26 link with `v=s3.1.26` deleted by hand. Hardened anyway: builders trim the version and drop `v` entirely when empty, Display board links never get `v`, the floqai-page fallback never leaves a dangling `?`, and `patron-portal-app.js` / `admin-app.js` / `floqr-session-shell.js` stamp `FLOQRNav.appVersion` instead of old literals. `app-version-sync.test.js` evaluates every FloqAi link (repository + product + help intents) with the package, with `""`/whitespace, and with no nav: always `?v=<package>` first, never `?&`, `v=&`, an empty `v`, or `v` on a board.

s3.1.37 (owner decision Oct 10 2026, supersedes the two paragraphs above): page links never carry `v` at all — FloqAi links are `./scheduling.html?from=floqai`, the notify redirect no longer sets `v`, and an incoming `v` is ignored. Only asset tags are cache-busted (bump script). `app-version-sync.test.js` now fails on **any** `v=` page link. `admin-scheduling.js` (never edit) still mints `v` on its own links — exempt in the test.

Embedded hint (s3.1.36): the shell's signed-out embed hint is a `floqr-session-hint` status line (`data-keep-visible`, `session.*` i18n keys), not `p.sub.small`, so `helper-popouts.js` never turns it into a `?` on the hero h1. `helper-popouts.js` also skips anything inside `[data-floqr-auth-chrome]`, and `FLOQRHelpAttach.attachBesideHeading` refuses an h1 target (the paragraph stays visible) — this also fixed `mingl-gist.html`. Test: `functions/session-hint-hero-help.test.js`.
